From: Monea Software <build@hdsatelit.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] GStreamer: hdsdvb gives the stream time of the board decoder after a seek (MSE) and keeps the position at the seek target until the board shows a new picture

With the hdsdvb quirk the position comes from the board decoder (get-decoder-time). Measured on the Octagon SF8008
(Shaka Player, Media Source Extensions, a seek to 60 s after 12 s of playback): the board showed 56 s to 68 s
(its PTS), but the page got 1.3 s to 12 s and stopped there, so the player waited for data around 12 s and the film
stopped when the buffered range 56-68 s ran out.

1. dvbmediasink gives PTS - (segment start - segment position), and WebKitMediaSrc sends segments with start = time =
   the seek target and position 0: the decoder time counts from the segment start. For Media Source Extensions the
   position is that time plus the segment time of the board sink whose decoder answered.
2. After a flushing seek the decoder keeps the time of the last picture shown before the flush until a new picture
   is shown, and the key unit seek starts at the key frame before the target. Until the decoder gives a new time
   (different from the one read when the seek started) that is not before the target, the position stays at the
   seek target, for playbin and for Media Source Extensions (not for reverse playback; a seek that fails turns it off).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [satellite receiver configuration]

